}
<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level5-standard-error> {
  ex:l5-s15a-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-standard-error ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-s15a-heading, ex:l5-s15a-plot, ex:l5-s15a-math ; cd:narration "We have examined environmental sampling variation. Now isolate the separate laboratory contribution, using the original five constructed repeats of one homogeneous nitrate sample: 9.6, 9.8, 10.0, 10.2 and 10.4 mg/L. These are not five field sites and must not be relabelled as environmental units. Their mean is 10.0 mg/L; the marker is not a sixth measurement. Deviations minus 0.4, minus 0.2, zero, plus 0.2 and plus 0.4 have squared sum 0.40 in squared concentration units. Dividing by five minus one gives sample variance 0.10 and sample SD about 0.316 mg/L. This SD describes individual analytical results, not a confidence-interval half-width or total uncertainty in the water-body mean. The detail axis near 10 mg/L is not the C14 environmental-population comparison. Next examine how this analytical variation propagates into a laboratory mean estimate."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15b-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-standard-error ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-s15b-heading, ex:l5-s15b-text, ex:l5-s15b-plot ; cd:narration "Keep the laboratory level explicit. This separate normal teaching model has analytical mean 10 mg/L and SD the square root of 0.10, about 0.316 mg/L. It is not the preceding lognormal population with SD 9, nor the earlier specified analytical SD 0.30. Matching the five-value example's scale is a deliberate model choice, not knowledge of the true population SD. Simulate five thousand independent laboratory series, each with five measurements and one mean. The bars describe those means; the line remains the individual analytical density. Their theoretical sampling SD is about 0.141421 mg/L; the realized simulation need not match exactly. All five thousand means fall within 8.8 to 11.2 mg/L, while the model tails extend beyond. This does not resample the original five values or establish a fitted curve as truth. The laboratory mean is exactly normal under the specified iid normal model, not because the CLT guarantees normality at size five. The next step estimates its SE from the five constructed laboratory values, not from an environmental sample."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15c-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-standard-error ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-s15c-heading, ex:l5-s15c-plot, ex:l5-s15c-math ; cd:narration "For iid observations with finite variance, true SE is population SD divided by the square root of sample size. Here the observations are laboratory repeats. Replace the unknown population SD by sample SD to get an estimated standard error, marked by the hat. The unrounded square root of 0.10 divided by the square root of five gives 0.141421 mg/L, about 0.141. The bars distinguish individual analytical spread from estimated precision of the laboratory mean. Neither is a confidence interval, a guaranteed error bound, or all measurement uncertainty. Most importantly, 0.141 mg/L is not the environmental SE of the water-body estimate. That requires the selected environmental units, their design, possible weighting and dependence. A different laboratory series changes both estimated SD and SE. Student-t will account for estimated spread under a normal model; it cannot supply missing environmental sampling information."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15d-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-standard-error ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-s15d-heading, ex:l5-s15d-list ; cd:narration "Our estimate needs more than small random error. In this separate hypothetical analytical-bias example, true reference concentration 10.0 mg/L plus a constant bias 0.2 gives expected result 10.2. Averaging five or eighty independent laboratory measurements keeps the expected mean at 10.2 while reducing its SD from about 0.1414 to 0.03536 mg/L. This is not a diagnosis of bias in the original five values. Selection bias is different: repeatedly analysing water taken only from one unrepresentative location cannot estimate the whole water body merely by increasing laboratory repeats. Technical repeats are not independent environmental samples. Correlation also changes variance of a mean through pairwise covariances, including off-diagonal terms. Calibration, reference-value and preparation uncertainty remain additional contributions. Neither the CLT nor a smaller SE corrects bias, creates environmental representativeness or repairs dependence. We next examine uncertainty in the estimated variance itself."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15a-heading a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15a-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15a-plot a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15a-chart ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15a-math a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15a-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15b-heading a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15b-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15b-text a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15b-context ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15b-plot a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15b-chart ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15c-heading a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15c-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15c-plot a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15c-chart ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15c-math a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15c-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15d-heading a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15d-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-s15d-list a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-s15d-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
